> anything, kind of like the word of GOD...
> - Is there a way to define CFLAGS and other compiler related
> flags so they override anything in any file?
> - Does the globally defined (env var) CFALGS have higher authority
> than the various config files?
> - What manual covers this?
> 
> wbr
> /levente

Like other poster stated, thats how you can change you CFLAGS setting..
you can also export them as well. When you get to know your CFLAGS, you
can take optimization to the next level... compiling everything
specifically for your processor ;-)

CFLAGS="-O3 -finline -fstrict-aliasing -fomit-frame-pointer -mtune=<cpu>
-mieee -pipe" ./configure

The "-mieee" turns on precision math, with out it some programs will
either crash or generate a floating point error... Most run just fine
without it thought.

The "-finline" for on lining of functions and the like

"-fstrict-aliasing" generates faster code as well [similar to
-ansi_alias with Compaq C"


You can also specify the Compiler and PreProcessor:
*for GCC
CC=gcc CXX=g++ CPP=cpp

*for Compaq C
CC=ccc CXX=cxx

Will L G


